<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=tofu">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Farming and food</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tofu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as bean curd, doufu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tofu, or bean curd, is a food made by pressing the curds of coagulated soy milk into solid blocks. It originated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, where its making was first recorded during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, and it has been eaten for over 2,000 years. A stone mural unearthed in 1960 from an Eastern Han tomb supports a Han origin. Tofu did not become a popular food in China until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>. It reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> with Zen Buddhist monks, and an offering of tofu at the Kasuga Shrine in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> is recorded in 1183. A Javanese inscription of 902 CE lists bean curd among foods at a feast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tofu.jpg" alt="Tofu" width="330" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DryPot · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_SilkyTofu_(Kinugoshi_Tofu).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>Han dynasty</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>China</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Chinese legend ascribes tofu to Prince Liu An (179 to 122 BCE) of Anhui province, though reliable sources for the period are few. Some scholars hold that tofu under the Han was rudimentary and lacked the firmness to count as tofu.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/soybean">Soybean<span>c. 7000 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=tofu">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
